examples.question_text:
Evaluate $\int_{1}^{3}(x-5)\,dx$. The shaded region shows the interval of integration.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{regionblue}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[regionblue] (1,0) -- (1,-4) -- (3,-2) -- (3,0) -- cycle;
\draw[black,->] (-0.4,0) -- (4.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-5.2) -- (0,1) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick] (0.3,-4.7) -- (4,-1);
\draw[black,dashed] (1,0) -- (1,-4);
\draw[black,dashed] (3,0) -- (3,-2);
\path (1,0) node[above,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$1$};
\path (3,0) node[above,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$3$};
\path (2,-4.8) node {$y=x-5$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
